      "bookmarked": false,
      "raw": "<p>I seem to remember seeing specific rules on when to reshuffle the trash upon emptying a deck, but I can&#39;t seem to find them anymore.</p><p>1) Do I reshuffle the trash when I need to &quot;reveal&quot; cards from an empty deck?</p><p>2) Do I reshuffle when I&#39;m asked to &quot;discard&quot; from an empty deck?</p><p>3) If my deck becomes empty, do I reshuffle immediately, or do I wait until I need to draw/reveal/discard from that deck?</p><p>I know this sounds nitpicky, but I&#39;ve been in situations where it matters. Like, &quot;Reveal cards until X equipment is found,&quot; when there&#39;s only 1 Equipment card left in the deck and I know I&#39;d have to reshuffle the trash to get enough to fulfill the card.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Oh, and in a related question, when asked to generally put a card from the trash back into a deck, or in play (say, from Simulation Room, placing a villain target from trash into play), how do I choose which card to place? Do I take the most recently discarded/destroyed target? Choose randomly? Or put in whichever one the players agree to put in?</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
